---
layout: null
sitemap: false
---
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
{% comment %}
Custom feed template overriding jekyll-feed's default (the plugin skips
generation when this file exists). Based on jekyll-feed v0.17.0 feed.xml:
that is the version the GitHub Pages builder pins in production (see
https://pages.github.com/versions.json) — the Gemfile only affects local
builds and may list a different version.

Posts on this site are dated with the *event* date, which is usually in the
future when the post is announced. RSS readers hide entries whose
<published>/<updated> lie in the future, so we clamp both to the build time
(site.time). Once the event date has passed, the entry reverts to the event
date, matching the old feed.
{% endcomment %}
<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom">
  <generator uri="https://jekyllrb.com/" version="{{ jekyll.version }}">Jekyll</generator>
  <link href="{{ page.url | absolute_url }}" rel="self" type="application/atom+xml" />
  <link href="{{ '/' | absolute_url }}" rel="alternate" type="text/html" />
  <updated>{{ site.time | date_to_xmlschema }}</updated>
  <id>{{ page.url | absolute_url | xml_escape }}</id>
  <title type="html">{{ site.title | smartify | xml_escape }}</title>
  {% if site.description %}
  <subtitle>{{ site.description | xml_escape }}</subtitle>
  {% endif %}
  {% assign posts = site.posts %}
  {% unless site.show_drafts %}
    {% assign posts = posts | where_exp: "post", "post.draft != true" %}
  {% endunless %}
  {% assign posts = posts | sort: "date" | reverse %}
  {% assign posts_limit = site.feed.posts_limit | default: 10 %}
  {% comment %}
  #62 changed the entry id format, which would resurface historical posts in
  readers as new items. Drop them from the feed instead.
  {% endcomment %}
  {% assign feed_start = '2026-08-01' | date: '%s' | plus: 0 %}
  {% for post in posts limit: posts_limit %}
    {% assign post_epoch = post.date | date: '%s' | plus: 0 %}
    {% if post_epoch < feed_start %}{% break %}{% endif %}
    {% if post.date > site.time %}
      {% assign entry_date = site.time %}
    {% else %}
      {% assign entry_date = post.date %}
    {% endif %}
    <entry>
      {% assign post_title = post.title | smartify | strip_html | normalize_whitespace | xml_escape %}
      <title type="html">{{ post_title }}</title>
      <link href="{{ post.url | absolute_url }}" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="{{ post_title }}" />
      <published>{{ entry_date | date_to_xmlschema }}</published>
      <updated>{{ post.last_modified_at | default: entry_date | date_to_xmlschema }}</updated>
      {% comment %}
      A tag: URI (RFC 4151) is unique (post.url embeds the event date and
      slug) and stays valid if the site ever moves domains.
      {% endcomment %}
      <id>tag:bitdevsamsterdam.org,{{ post.date | date: "%Y" }}:{{ post.url | xml_escape }}</id>
      <content type="html" xml:base="{{ post.url | absolute_url | xml_escape }}"><![CDATA[{{ post.content | strip }}]]></content>
      {% assign post_author = post.author | default: site.author %}
      <author>
        <name>{{ post_author.name | default: post_author | default: "" | xml_escape }}</name>
      </author>
      {% assign post_summary = post.description | default: post.excerpt %}
      {% if post_summary and post_summary != empty %}
      <summary type="html"><![CDATA[{{ post_summary | strip_html | normalize_whitespace }}]]></summary>
      {% endif %}
    </entry>
  {% endfor %}
</feed>
